.TH "selectronic_nut_poller" 1 "Thu Sep 24 2026" "selectronic-nut-poller" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
selectronic_nut_poller \- selectronic-nut-poller - poll a Selectronic SP PRO and publish NUT values 

.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.PP
.nf
SELECTRONIC_IP=INVERTER_IP SELECTRONIC_DEVICE_ID=DEVICE_ID \
selectronic-nut-poller
.fi
.PP
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Performs one poll of the Selectronic SP PRO local HTTP JSON point endpoint and atomically writes a NUT dummy-ups definition file\&. The container invokes it repeatedly\&. A failed poll returns a non-zero status so the caller can retain the last valid NUT data\&.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.PP
Required: SELECTRONIC_IP and SELECTRONIC_DEVICE_ID\&.
.PP
Optional: SELECTRONIC_MODEL (default SP PRO), SELECTRONIC_SERIAL, NUT_DEFINITION_FILE (default /etc/nut/selectronic\&.dev), SELECTRONIC_BATTERY_CAPACITY_KWH (default 0), SELECTRONIC_RUNTIME_EFFICIENCY (default 0\&.9), SELECTRONIC_INVERTER_CAPACITY_KW (default 5\&.0), SELECTRONIC_SOLAR_CAPACITY_KW (default 0), SELECTRONIC_AC_VOLTAGE (default 240), SELECTRONIC_BATTERY_VOLTAGE (default 0), SELECTRONIC_SHUTDOWN_PERCENT (default 10), SELECTRONIC_LOW_BATTERY (default 20), and SELECTRONIC_AC_MODE (default always_online)\&.
.SH "OUTPUT"
.PP
Writes standard NUT values and Selectronic telemetry to the configured dummy-ups definition file using an atomic temporary-file rename\&.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
Returns 0 on success and non-zero when configuration, HTTP, JSON, or file output processing fails\&.
.SH "EXAMPLE"
.PP
.PP
.nf
SELECTRONIC_IP=192\&.0\&.2\&.10 SELECTRONIC_DEVICE_ID=DEVICE_ID \
SELECTRONIC_BATTERY_CAPACITY_KWH=10 selectronic-nut-poller
.fi
.PP
 
